@echo off
rem asight collector: launcher for VS Code on Windows (RFC 4.8 s2.4), written by the VS Code opt-in item of
rem `asight on kimi-code --opt-in kimi-code.vscode`. Your VS Code shortcut starts this instead of Code.exe: it sets
rem the CA file Node reads (the asight CA, plus any CA you already gave Kimi Code) for every extension of the
rem editor and runs the real Code.exe. The proxy itself is VS Code's own http.proxy setting, not this environment.
rem `asight off kimi-code` removes it.
set "NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=__ASIGHT_CA_FILE__"
"__ASIGHT_REAL_BINARY__" %*
